    "prespecified": "Fixed 2026-11-20, before any result of these profiles was read (owner's redefinition of #482).\nGate:\n- no config_error; one binary; every cell records world breeders-x4 with the same borg_world_data_sha256 in every arm;\n- each arm's policy value in borg.txt and in params-core.json;\n- the arms must play differently: at least p0 and p2 differ from p3 in some games. If an arm is identical to p3 in\n  all 18 pilot games, stop and report it before the larger tiers;\n- every cell ends in death, turn_cap or borg_stopped (exit 2 means the world was not applied); frozen-turn bursts\n  classified; death bundles reproduced with the same world.\nReport per arm and per class: deaths and causes, final and maximum level, deepest level; breeder deaths (the killer\nhas MULTIPLY); paired rescued and newly killed against p3 (exact McNemar) and games identical to p3; breeders created\nand killed per game; per game \"# Breeders cannot be stopped\", \"No rest: ... breeders known\" and the flees from a lost\nlevel; mean max CL and DL against p3 with non-inferiority at #347's margins (CL -0.25, DL -0.25); a RULES 18 bin for\neach arm. A breeder world is a stress test: a level that wins here still needs normal play's measurement (#460)\nbefore its shipped value changes.",
